From 2fefe24f4713820421b6f60b7d897381dd1eeb45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:06:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: Dismiss and "Clear all failed" stick (server hiddenAt);
 copy fixes on the Queue and Suite
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Queue Dismiss called nothing on the server (an in-memory set), so every failure came back on
  the next launch. It now calls DELETE /v1/jobs/:id; "Clear all failed" calls
  POST /v1/jobs/clear-failed.
- "you weren't charged · you weren't charged": ScreenCopy.failure says it once.
- Retry price is the server's price for the job (cost), not a local estimate; Suite "Retry free"
  -> "Retry · $price", hub badge "Not charged".
- Templates: starters say "by MUSE" and "Starter", not "by You" / "Public".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Py2rxp4Ymtv7wd2xgwL5P1
